# Canonical generated workspace under .cache

Move regenerable extraction, FBX conversion, Unreal staging, build
intermediates, logs, and decision data out of the repository root into one
documented `.cache/` hierarchy; keep `game/` as user-supplied source evidence
and `dist/` as final copied output instead of introducing an ambiguous
generated `assets/` root.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Migrate `extracted/`, `fbx-assets/`, `unreal-staging/`, build
  intermediates, logs, and transient decision files to stable `.cache/`
  subpaths with compatibility handling for existing local workspaces.
- [ ] Update commands, manifests, tests, documentation, and validators so
  root-level legacy generated directories are no longer authoritative.
- [x] Keep `game/` outside `.cache/` because it is user-supplied source evidence
  and keep `dist/` outside `.cache/` because it is the final user
  deliverable.
- [ ] Preserve resumability, provenance, deterministic hashes, and transaction
  recovery while moving paths.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency is required beyond the declared repository and
platform prerequisites.

## Evidence

The supported build tools keep user-supplied `game/` outside `.cache`, use
`.cache/build/data/` for versioned decisions, `.cache/build/cargo-*` for Cargo
state, and `.cache/build/run/<target>/` for Turnkey reports, UAT/UBA logs,
staging candidates, and platform build evidence. Final publication remains
`dist/<target-id>/`; no generic generated `assets/` root is introduced.

A real Windows AMD64 cook verified `UE-LocalDataCachePath` with Zen data rooted
under `.cache/build/run/windows-x64/build-hermetic-test/ddc/Zen`; UAT logs were
also redirected under that build workspace. The migration adapters still own
physical root-level `extracted/`, `fbx-assets/`, and `unreal-staging/` defaults,
and Unreal itself still uses project `Saved/`/`Intermediate/` during cook. Those
surfaces remain open and must be migrated coherently without changing logical
manifest identities such as `extracted/...`.
